            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 81-year-old male patient, admitted on 19/02/2026 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Blood tests revealed mild systemic inflammation. He was promptly treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and closely monitored vital signs throughout his stay. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge. We recommend close follow-up and continuation of optimised inhaler therapy. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you require further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
